00:29:29.784 --> 00:29:31.200
And we're going
to use that Vision

00:29:31.200 --> 00:29:34.080
API to detect if
an image is violent

00:29:34.080 --> 00:29:36.000
or adult image or
something like that

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:40.230
and prevent that student
from uploading that image.

00:29:40.230 --> 00:29:42.600
And then finally I want
to add some fun facts

00:29:42.600 --> 00:29:45.480
about the student, so something
interesting about the student.

00:29:45.480 --> 00:29:48.480
But I want to make this
so that student can speak,

00:29:48.480 --> 00:29:50.540
and we will detect
from their voice,

00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:52.720
and we will convert
that to text,

00:29:52.720 --> 00:29:55.680
and then we will enter
that as fun facts.

00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:57.870
Doing this on your own,
it's not that easy.

00:29:57.870 --> 00:29:59.620
But I can use something
called Speech API.

00:29:59.620 --> 00:30:02.250
It's another machine learning
API where you can basically

00:30:02.250 --> 00:30:04.650
pass in a file with
some sound and then

00:30:04.650 --> 00:30:06.450
it extracts the text for you.

00:30:06.450 --> 00:30:09.490
So that's what I want to
add to my application.

00:30:09.490 --> 00:30:11.370
So let's take a look
at our code again.

00:30:18.870 --> 00:30:24.460
All right, so what I'm
going to show you is,

00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:27.250
first let's look at
the profile picture.

00:30:27.250 --> 00:30:30.188
So let me just find
the code for that.

00:30:35.020 --> 00:30:38.210
First I created a service.

00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:40.640
And I called it ImageUploader.

00:30:40.640 --> 00:30:43.890
So this is a really
simple service.

00:30:43.890 --> 00:30:47.432
Let's see if you can
see that properly.

00:30:47.432 --> 00:30:49.390
So this service, one
thing you're going to note

00:30:49.390 --> 00:30:53.260
is that it's using
Google Cloud Storage.

00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:55.960
This is a NuGet library
that you can reference

00:30:55.960 --> 00:30:57.370
from your application.

00:30:57.370 --> 00:31:00.160
And with that, you get
access to Cloud Storage.

00:31:00.160 --> 00:31:03.700
And this ImageUploader,
it basically

00:31:03.700 --> 00:31:05.680
takes in a bucket name,
because in clusters you

00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:09.010
need to have a bucket
to save images.

00:31:09.010 --> 00:31:11.761
And then it creates
a StorageClient.

00:31:11.761 --> 00:31:13.510
So this is the guy
that we're going to use

00:31:13.510 --> 00:31:16.090
to talk to Cloud Storage.

00:31:16.090 --> 00:31:17.480
And then it has two methods.

00:31:17.480 --> 00:31:20.210
One method is
called UploadImage.

00:31:20.210 --> 00:31:22.390
And the other one is
called DeleteImage.

00:31:22.390 --> 00:31:24.100
Because when you
delete the student,

00:31:24.100 --> 00:31:26.240
you want to delete
the image as well.

00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:30.200
So the UploadImage, it
basically takes in an image

00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:31.670
and it takes in an ID.

00:31:31.670 --> 00:31:33.470
So this is the ID of a student.

00:31:33.470 --> 00:31:36.820
And it uses Cloud Storage
to upload the image.

00:31:36.820 --> 00:31:39.910
And it basically just
says, take this image,

00:31:39.910 --> 00:31:42.400
save it to this
bucket with this ID.

00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:43.940
And then this is the source.

00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:46.420
And make sure that the
image is publicly readable.

00:31:46.420 --> 00:31:50.060
So with one call you can upload
the image to Cloud Storage.

00:31:50.060 --> 00:31:53.750
And then if you look at
the DeleteUploadedImage,

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:56.120
again it takes in an ID
and then uses StorageClient

00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:57.470
to delete the image.

00:31:57.470 --> 00:31:58.760
So it's very basic.

00:31:58.760 --> 00:32:01.280
And what I also
changed is that if you

00:32:01.280 --> 00:32:09.419
look at student controller,
I added an ImageUploader.

00:32:09.419 --> 00:32:11.460
And I'm going to talk
about the SafeImageUploader

00:32:11.460 --> 00:32:13.200
in a little bit.

00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:18.167
And then if you look
here for example,

00:32:18.167 --> 00:32:19.250
this is the Create method.

00:32:19.250 --> 00:32:22.340
This is when the
student is created.

00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:26.240
What we are doing is if
an image has been passed,

00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:30.170
then use ImageUploader to upload
that image with the student ID.

00:32:30.170 --> 00:32:32.590
And then this will
return you a path.

00:32:32.590 --> 00:32:34.310
It's a public URL basically.

00:32:34.310 --> 00:32:37.070
And that will set that as
the student image path.

00:32:37.070 --> 00:32:39.650
So with that, we can
have profile pictures.

00:32:39.650 --> 00:32:41.690
So let me just show
you how this works.

00:32:44.920 --> 00:32:45.600
This is the one.

00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:47.730
So I have it running
locally already.

00:32:47.730 --> 00:32:49.290
I'll go to students.

00:32:49.290 --> 00:32:52.170
And let's just
create a new student.

00:32:52.170 --> 00:32:55.920
And I'll just add
myself as a student.

00:32:55.920 --> 00:32:58.200
I'll talk about fun
facts afterwards.

00:32:58.200 --> 00:32:59.999
But let's just choose a picture.

00:32:59.999 --> 00:33:01.290
I'll choose one of my pictures.

00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:09.950
And let me just
change just to 2017.

00:33:09.950 --> 00:33:11.416
Hit Create.

00:33:11.416 --> 00:33:13.040
So this will basically
take my picture,

00:33:13.040 --> 00:33:16.680
upload it to Cloud Storage,
and then save it as image path.

00:33:16.680 --> 00:33:19.780
And if I look at the
student list, I am here.

00:33:19.780 --> 00:33:24.620
And if I look at the
details, I have a picture.

00:33:24.620 --> 00:33:29.750
OK, that's good, but having
these pictures for each student

00:33:29.750 --> 00:33:31.310
and uploading them
one by one, it's

00:33:31.310 --> 00:33:33.014
going to take a while, right?

00:33:33.014 --> 00:33:34.430
So what I want to
do now is I want

00:33:34.430 --> 00:33:39.300
to use PowerShell cmdlets
that we have to script this,

00:33:39.300 --> 00:33:43.160
so that we can upload a
bunch of images all at once.

00:33:43.160 --> 00:33:45.450
When you install
Google Cloud SDK,

00:33:45.450 --> 00:33:47.780
you have these
cmdlets by default.

00:33:47.780 --> 00:33:50.640
So you have them by default.
So I have it here already.

00:33:50.640 --> 00:33:54.330
So let me just show you
this PowerShell cmdlet.

00:33:54.330 --> 00:33:56.540
So it's called upload pictures.

00:33:56.540 --> 00:34:00.210
And then it also has a picture
folder right next to it.

00:34:00.210 --> 00:34:02.280
So what we're doing here
is that I have a bucket.

00:34:02.280 --> 00:34:05.400
So this is the bucket that I
want to save in Cloud Storage.

00:34:05.400 --> 00:34:07.800
And this is my
folder of pictures.

00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:10.080
And all I'm saying is
that New-GcsObject.

00:34:10.080 --> 00:34:12.900
So Gcs stands for
Google Cloud Storage.

00:34:12.900 --> 00:34:15.210
So basically what
this command does

00:34:15.210 --> 00:34:20.580
is take this folder and
upload to this bucket,

00:34:20.580 --> 00:34:23.050
and make sure that they
are publicly readable.

00:34:23.050 --> 00:34:26.190
And then I do this
by New-GcsObject.

00:34:26.190 --> 00:34:28.590
And then basically
just run this.

00:34:28.590 --> 00:34:31.380
And let's just do that
and see how that looks.

00:34:35.800 --> 00:34:39.010
So this is working.

00:34:39.010 --> 00:34:41.870
In here, if I can
show you, there's

00:34:41.870 --> 00:34:47.860
a bunch of other cmdlets, like
Add-GcsBucket, Add-GcsObject.

00:34:47.860 --> 00:34:50.110
So these are all
Google Cloud PowerShell

00:34:50.110 --> 00:34:52.857
cmdlets that you can
use in your scripting.

00:34:52.857 --> 00:34:54.940
As you can see, it's already
looking at the images

00:34:54.940 --> 00:34:56.150
and uploading them.

00:34:56.150 --> 00:34:59.500
And if we go back
to our console,

00:34:59.500 --> 00:35:05.460
and I go to here
and Cloud Storage,

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:07.380
I have a bunch of buckets
for all my projects.

00:35:07.380 --> 00:35:10.720
But the one I care
about is called Contoso.

00:35:10.720 --> 00:35:12.630
I click here.

00:35:12.630 --> 00:35:15.510
And you can see that the
folder is already uploaded

00:35:15.510 --> 00:35:17.520
with a bunch of pictures.

00:35:17.520 --> 00:35:20.100
And I can use these
pictures, change my code

00:35:20.100 --> 00:35:24.900
so that they can refer to these
pictures and just use them.

00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:27.210
So the next thing
I want to show you

00:35:27.210 --> 00:35:31.430
is, so these pictures can
be anything right now.

00:35:31.430 --> 00:35:33.480
So a student can upload
any kind of picture.

00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:34.650
And we want to prevent that.

00:35:34.650 --> 00:35:36.816
We want to make sure these
pictures are not violent,

00:35:36.816 --> 00:35:38.820
they're not adult pictures.

00:35:38.820 --> 00:35:42.450
So to do that, I want
to use Vision API.

00:35:42.450 --> 00:35:46.520
So let me go back to code again.

00:35:46.520 --> 00:35:51.930
What I did is I created
another service called

00:35:51.930 --> 00:35:53.490
ImageSafetyChecker.

00:35:53.490 --> 00:35:56.670
So this guy, I get first--

00:35:56.670 --> 00:36:02.330
oh, come on.

00:36:02.330 --> 00:36:07.070
This guy, it's using
the Vision API library.

00:36:07.070 --> 00:36:09.680
So it's a NuGet package
again that you can install.

00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:15.000
And then it has a client again
called ImageAnnotatorClient.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:18.350
So this is a client that you
use to talk to Vision API.

00:36:18.350 --> 00:36:20.240
So when we create this
ImageSafetyChecker,

00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:21.950
we create the client as well.

00:36:21.950 --> 00:36:24.740
And then it has a simple
method called IsSafe.

00:36:24.740 --> 00:36:29.450
So given a file,
this takes this file,

00:36:29.450 --> 00:36:34.130
and then passes it to
the ImageAnnotatorClient,

00:36:34.130 --> 00:36:34.920
right here.

00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:37.670
And this basically
calls Vision API

00:36:37.670 --> 00:36:40.940
and gets some annotations
about that image.

00:36:40.940 --> 00:36:44.300
And then the annotations, they
have four dimensions, adult,

00:36:44.300 --> 00:36:46.310
violent, spoof, or medical.

00:36:46.310 --> 00:36:49.850
So what I'm doing here is
that-- and these annotations,

00:36:49.850 --> 00:36:50.780
they're enums.

00:36:50.780 --> 00:36:54.320
So they can change
from very unlikely,

00:36:54.320 --> 00:36:58.160
to unlikely, possible,
likely, or very unlikely.

00:36:58.160 --> 00:37:00.170
So given an image, it
basically tells you

00:37:00.170 --> 00:37:03.800
this image is very likely that
it's an adult image, or very

00:37:03.800 --> 00:37:05.967
unlikely that it's a violent
image, stuff like that.

00:37:05.967 --> 00:37:07.841
So what I'm doing here
is that I am basically

00:37:07.841 --> 00:37:09.514
just checking all
the dimensions,

00:37:09.514 --> 00:37:11.180
and making sure that
their likelihood is

00:37:11.180 --> 00:37:13.054
less than possible, so
that it's not possible

00:37:13.054 --> 00:37:16.190
that they're adult or violence.

00:37:16.190 --> 00:37:22.089
So this method will basically
give me the safety that I need.

00:37:22.089 --> 00:37:23.630
And then what I did
is that, remember

00:37:23.630 --> 00:37:26.600
we had the ImageUploader
to upload our images?

00:37:26.600 --> 00:37:29.660
I created another one
called SafeImageUploader.

00:37:29.660 --> 00:37:33.300
And it extends
from ImageUploader.

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:35.580
And then the only
thing that it adds

00:37:35.580 --> 00:37:38.790
is that it basically
has a reference

00:37:38.790 --> 00:37:41.530
to this ImageSafetyChecker.

00:37:41.530 --> 00:37:46.820
And when we upload the image,
instead of uploading that image

00:37:46.820 --> 00:37:50.690
right away, we call the
ImageSafetyChecker and ask,

00:37:50.690 --> 00:37:51.980
is this image safe?

00:37:51.980 --> 00:37:54.587
If it's not safe, we
throw an exception.

00:37:54.587 --> 00:37:56.420
And then otherwise we
just upload the image.

00:37:56.420 --> 00:38:00.170
So with this, I have the safety
that I need to upload my image.

00:38:00.170 --> 00:38:03.980
And then if we go to
StudentController,

00:38:03.980 --> 00:38:07.350
I show you before,
instead of creating

00:38:07.350 --> 00:38:11.330
a regular ImageUploader, I'm
creating a SafeImageUploader.

00:38:11.330 --> 00:38:13.860
So by default I'm using
the safety feature.

00:38:13.860 --> 00:38:16.350
Now let me just show
you how that works.

00:38:16.350 --> 00:38:17.784
So go back to my app.

00:38:20.510 --> 00:38:22.320
I think it was this one.

